 check/PUT, outside the uncertain-effect try. A projection overflow therefore causes no remote mutation and is not mistaken for an uncertain accepted write. The cap is not increased and names are not dropped to make room. No-op/current-set behavior and <=1000 replacement remain intact. Each convergence effect uses one complete sorted PUT, with fresh snapshots between attempts.\",\n    \"full_label_reads\": \"Explicit100-item numbered GET pages, at most11 calls with a terminal empty/short page,1000-name aggregate limit, strict list/object/name types and unique nonempty <=100-character names reject malformed/repeated/overflow/read failures. Exact1000 checks terminal page11 rather than silently truncating. Test PagedGitHub and new paired AtomicGitHub implement actual explicit paging; generic small-case fakes remain scoped to their short lists.\",\n    \"lock_and_deadlines\": \"Existing per-state/repository/PR reentrant lock and POSIX file-lock behavior remain unchanged; there is no new global worker lock. Additional operations are bounded by30 seconds/24 iterations with a budget check before each read/mutation. Existing in-flight command timeout180 seconds is not a hard30-second total; source/plan correctly leave that transport limit distinct. Existing worker busy-origin recognition remains compatible.\",\n    \"freshness_and_activity\": \"Snapshots check expected open/closed state and exact head, obtain full labels, classify current private attention and rerun the supplied projection. Immediately before mutation a second full snapshot refreshes labels/attention/actual callback observations. Each successful mutation returns to fresh snapshot/projection checks before convergence. A head/state mismatch aborts without adopting the old decision for a new head. Supplied worker callback reads live Futures but captures an earlier pending-request inventory; no global fresh task/private activity CAS is invented.\",\n    \"owner_attention\": \"Current owner/security/provenance/veto/question attention dominates a phase and can suppress its display while preserving Future/private ownership. Display code reads authority and does not process owner approval comments or clear holds. Closed cleanup preserves retained attention, and unknown choose=None ownership preserves the current phase except explicitly requested removal. Release removes only writing and keeps a new review phase.\",\n    \"uncertain_acknowledgment\": \"PUT errors or malformed response are treated as uncertain. A new authenticated full snapshot is obtained before considering convergence. An already applied exact current desired set can converge without another PUT; otherwise the original diagnostic propagates for ordinary later reconciliation. There is no blind stale restore, POST retry or capability downgrade. Valid-shaped but incorrect acknowledgment also cannot succeed without the next actual current snapshot.\",\n    \"races\": \"A one-request replacement removes this automation internal empty remove/add interval. No GitHub label-set CAS exists here: a noncooperating actor can still alter head/labels after final read or add an unrelated label that the PUT cannot atomically preserve. Source documentation and plan explicitly acknowledge the unavoidable independent-writer lost-update race and normal recovery for visible drift. No universal never-stale claim is granted.\",\n    \"real_worker_and_legacy\": \"The complete frozen worker labels.py is independently byte-equal to committed self_host426, SHA42094cd3. shared_transition chooses the concrete trusted capability; execution failure propagates and never falls back to DELETE/POST. Legacy controllers without it retain intentional existing legacy transition and closed cleanup behavior. This source feature cannot claim those legacy deployments already fixed.\",\n    \"plan_caller_difference\": \"The approved plan source path still hashes150ef33b/14870 bytes; it adds only controller-compatibility to the readonly reviewing-role branch. The frozen actual426 caller42094/14840 lacks that unpublished mapping. Its shared function signature/dispatch/acquire/reconcile semantics are unchanged; this assessment binds actual426, not the unpublished admission workspace. Future admission-successor compatibility must separately bind its exact source.\",\n    \"test_helper_extraction\": \"The complete current shared label_api.py and label_reconciliation.py were freshly reread. The extracted GitHub facade, PUT replacement/legacy branches and hooks are unchanged. Moving the label_api import before github_agent remains acyclic: label_api imports github_agent, which does not import label_reconciliation; subsequent import uses its initialized module. Formatting of the merge-mutation comprehension preserves the exact filter/output. Exception message variables retain exact class/text/args and raise boundaries. No failure is swallowed or assertion loosened.\",\n    \"new_and_cumulative_tests\": \"All3current changed test/helper bodies were freshly read completely. atomic_status retains the same cases and assertions, including the two genuine projected-overflow zero-write cases, full pagination, idempotence, loss/malformed acknowledgment and callback drift. r\\\"Projected.*capacity\\\" has precisely the same characters/pattern as the former ordinary string; only the lint raw-marker requirement changes. Slicing whitespace, signature wrapping, message-local assignments, blank lines and import sorting are semantically equivalent. Six other selected test/support bodies and both paired legacy tests remain byte-identical to cumulative full prior reads. No quota/test/authority baseline, expected effect or meaningful failure observation was weakened.\",\n    \"pairing_fixture\": \"The complete V2 fixture149229 bytes was parsed as inert data and both entire decoded source bodies matched current frozen source exactly: unchanged controller4ad and corrected review_control5b75. Same genuine new task/base/independent-plan-review metadata and explicit no-authority field retained. The full paired test body was reread; its only delta is EXPECTED review_control digest5f93->5b75. Thus the old rejected candidate source is not silently substituted for this V2 candidate.\",\n    \"documentation_and_fragment\": \"Relevant lifecycle operations documentation now explains complete PUT, unrelated-label preservation, uncertain-ack readback and independent-writer limits. The unique fragment records the actual behavior change; no package version or unrelated documentation rewrite is introduced.\"\n  },\n  \"exact_current_pair\": {\n    \"fixture_metadata\": {\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"repository\": \"Karapsin/analytics_toolkit\",\n      \"base\": \"f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01\",\n      \"task_id\": \"12c7a273d1c84f48bcb6abfb9e3c6caa\",\n      \"plan_review_sha256\": \"01964cec0f18de544b30be33e2783aebbb7fd9c0c9d38f78b393b76a6aa16a41\",\n      \"kind\": \"unpublished-atomic-controller-candidate-source-fixture\",\n      \"authority\": \"Full source fixture for local simulated paired tests only; no protected/published/source/operation approval\"\n    },\n    \"decoded_sources\": [\n      {\n        \"path\": \".github/agent/controller.py\",\n        \"bytes\": 57499,\n        \"sha256\": \"4ad12163c313fa3d8a05682081954ebc03ddb01052a65765cc908558572f5e4e\",\n        \"complete_source_byte_equal\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"path\": \".github/agent/review_control.py\",\n        \"bytes\": 53844,\n        \"sha256\": \"5b75b431f9768617e9bb75b6c9689a961a9bec4aa568a58ed0a9749af37143a6\",\n        \"complete_source_byte_equal\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"fake_transport_and_auth_explicit\": true,\n    \"current_live_authority_or_activation_inferred\": false\n  },\n  \"validation_evidence\": {\n    \"latest_mandatory_attempt\": {\n      \"managed_output\": {\n        \"blockers\": [\n          {\n            \"command\": \"release_routines/pre_commit_checks.sh --static\",\n            \"